F-4610 anchoring replay (J-3950), hot hub, Du down. (1) EMISSARY warranted (left_lane.py ~928): the 41% exact-0.0 is genuine rejection, not placeholder echo. The 288 logged 0.0 rows are those with EMPTY evidence ("(no lived evidence offered)"); replaying the 44 of them that retain old_self+candidate on gemma4:12b gave 0.0 on 220/220 calls across prefill 0.0, 1.0, 0.5, "<number>" text and omitted schema (key present every time). Rows WITH evidence (40 sampled x5 variants x2 reps = 400 calls) gave exact 0.0 zero times under any variant (means 0.41-0.46; A vs B identical on 62/80 pairs, mean abs diff 0.04). So prefill value does not move this judge; the 0.0 is driven by the no-evidence input, which also means a quarter-plus of the T4 emissary log is a constant-by-construction signal. (2) NARRATIVE score_llm agency/communion (qwen3.5:9b): anchorable. On 20 real both-0.0 passages (120-char text_head only, selected on the outcome, so exact-0 rates are biased up), prefill 0.0 -> 30% exact-0.0; 1.0 -> 50% exact-0.0 and only 5% 1.0; 0.5 -> 0% exact-0 and 50% exactly 0.5 echoed (mean 0.46); text placeholder -> 40% exact-0; omitted -> 20%. Agency and communion zero together in every exact-0 case. The 0.0 prefill is therefore not the sole cause of the both-0.0 rows (1.0 prefill gives even more zeros), but 0.5 prefill is copied half the time, so the example value does influence output on this site; the effect is small-sample (n=20 per arm) and passage-selection biased.
